1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,710
At two thirteen in the morning,

2
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:05,950
a drug dealer named Leo received a message
from an unknown number.

3
00:00:06,370 --> 00:00:07,660
One last delivery.

4
00:00:09,900 --> 00:00:12,300
One hundred thousand dollars. No
questions.

5
00:00:12,690 --> 00:00:15,320
Leo had been dealing drugs for seven
years.

6
00:00:15,650 --> 00:00:17,550
He'd never seen an offer like this.

7
00:00:18,060 --> 00:00:19,480
The pickup was simple.

8
00:00:19,750 --> 00:00:23,260
A black suitcase, waiting inside an
abandoned warehouse.

9
00:00:23,650 --> 00:00:26,400
He grabbed it and drove to the delivery
address.

10
00:00:26,830 --> 00:00:30,050
But when he arrived, his hands began
shaking.

11
00:00:31,270 --> 00:00:32,890
It was his childhood home.

12
00:00:33,380 --> 00:00:35,890
The house had been empty for fifteen
years.

13
00:00:36,590 --> 00:00:38,930
His phone buzzed. Go inside.

14
00:00:39,320 --> 00:00:41,560
Leo slowly opened the front door.

15
00:00:41,940 --> 00:00:45,520
In the living room sat an old television,
playing a recording.

16
00:00:45,950 --> 00:00:48,520
It showed Leo, seven years earlier,

17
00:00:48,820 --> 00:00:51,130
making his very first drug deal.

18
00:00:51,590 --> 00:00:54,080
Then another recording. And another.

19
00:00:54,440 --> 00:00:56,560
Every crime he'd ever committed.

20
00:00:56,960 --> 00:00:59,170
Suddenly, the television went black.

21
00:00:59,500 --> 00:01:02,740
White letters appeared. Open the suitcase.

22
00:01:03,340 --> 00:01:06,400
Leo unlatched it. There were no drugs.

23
00:01:06,590 --> 00:01:08,860
Only a photograph of his younger brother,

24
00:01:09,130 --> 00:01:11,810
who had died from an overdose three years
ago.

25
00:01:12,500 --> 00:01:14,520
Behind the photograph was a note.

26
00:01:14,860 --> 00:01:16,710
You sold him his first dose.

27
00:01:17,130 --> 00:01:18,050
Leo froze.

28
00:01:18,780 --> 00:01:19,840
His phone rang.

29
00:01:20,200 --> 00:01:22,280
He answered with trembling hands.

30
00:01:23,070 --> 00:01:24,620
A familiar voice whispered:

31
00:01:25,190 --> 00:01:26,150
Hello, big brother.

32
00:01:27,130 --> 00:01:28,380
Then the lights went out.

33
00:01:29,010 --> 00:01:30,880
And someone upstairs started walking.
